# Jaguar S-Type X200, 1999-2008.
#
# The 1999 S-Type revived a 1960s nameplate on an all-new retro-styled saloon, the
# first Jaguar of the Ford era, and shared nothing with the 1963 S-Type in this
# pakset. It was launched in March 1999 and built to 2008, growing slightly in 2002
# and again in 2006.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_S-Type_(1999)
#
# Dimensions 4.808 x 1.819 x 1.415 m, wheelbase 2.908 m: the 2000-2001 launch
# figures, converted from the published inches (189.3 x 71.6 x 55.7, wheelbase
# 114.5). The later lengths, 4.854 m for 2002-05 and 4.913 m for 2006-07, are
# recorded here but not modelled separately, since only the bumper and lamp
# treatment changed.
#
# Colours: Ebony, Silver, Mistral Blue and British Racing Green, Jaguar UK
# offerings of the launch period. The 1999-2005 shares are measured, so no era
# adjustment is needed: black 3, silver 3, blue 2, green 2. Total 10. Provisional
# pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 210 km/h, at the Rover 800 R17's tier: the volume engines were the 3.0 V6
# and the 4.0/4.2 V8. Comfort 110/345, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 110, equal to the
# Rover 800 and a step below the Rover 75's 105/340 range in ride terms. Class 3.
#
# Dates are road presence: March 1999 intro, retires staggered 2018-2024 on a
# nineteen- to twenty-five-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-s-type-x200.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-s-type-x200.dae (69 objects). References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-s-type-x200/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons,
# CC BY-SA 4.0: a true side elevation, front and rear of the same 2002 car).
#
# Accepted low-poly deviations, recorded rather than corrected: the geometry is a
# simplified and more angular interpretation of the photographed compound curves,
# and the 2004 facelift is a colour run on this master rather than a second shell.

obj=citycar
name=JaguarSTypeX200(Ebony)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1999
intro_month=3
retire_year=2020
retire_month=6
speed=210
class=3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=110
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=345

